  "releaseNotes": "LC026 now recognises a CancellationToken stored in a field or surfaced through a readable property as an available token, so an EF async call that omits it is flagged (and the fixer passes it by name) — previously only locals and parameters counted, silently missing the common injected-token / IHostApplicationLifetime.ApplicationStopping patterns. (Found by a second adversarial false-negative rescan.)",
